      "writtenOn": "2018-07-23T21:31:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure I understand this comment.\n1) The alignment of struct ap_reset_log_entry is 4, since that is the alignment of its widest component scalar type.\n\n2) If __packed was specified, then the alignment of member reset_time_ms would be incorrect on the odd-ordered members of recent_ap_reset.\n\nCan you provide an example of an EC + supported compiler that does not emit naturally aligned structures?",
      "parentUuid": "4231ef63_6ee2b0d6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 4832,
        "startChar": 3,
        "endLine": 4832,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "3caf659c9484bedab275606794337a0dc4c7d375",
